## Core Principle: Multi-Field Typeahead (Generic)

Typeahead is **not** a single-column name search. Wherever a user might type an **ID**, **code**, **email**, **domain**, **display name**, or **OCR text from uploaded images**, the suggestion query should match **all reasonable identifying fields**—as long as the UX stays smooth (debounced, capped list, merge/dedupe).

**Menu and listing must use the same fields.** Local `getSearchFields` / loaded-page filters cannot be richer than the committed list fetch. If the dropdown matches `title` / `name` / `location`, Enter must query those columns too — not only a denormalized blob.

### Denormalized `searchText` (optional blob, never the only criterion)

Entities with image OCR may store extracted text in `ocrText` / `ocr_text`, then fold it into **`searchText` / `search_text`**. Include **`searchText.contains` as one parallel job**. **Never** `ocrText.contains`. **Never** query `searchText.contains` alone for typeahead or the listing after Enter.

This repo does **not** ship `src/lib/search/buildSearchText.ts`. The blob is often empty, so a title like “Parsippany…” matches local `title` in the menu and then returns an empty grid if Enter only sends `searchText.contains`.

JHipster **ANDs** multiple `.contains` on one request. Run **one field per request**, then merge by `id` (`fetchPublicTypeahead` / `fetchPublicSearchPage`). Numeric queries also run `id.equals` when `/^\d+$/`.

### Public field lists (source of truth)

Use the constants in [`publicTypeaheadSearch.ts`](mdc:src/lib/publicTypeaheadSearch.ts) for both the dropdown and the committed page:

| Constant | Fields (parallel `.contains`) |
|----------|-------------------------------|
| `PUBLIC_EVENT_SEARCH_FIELDS` | `searchText`, `title`, `caption`, `description`, `location` |
| `PUBLIC_GALLERY_ALBUM_SEARCH_FIELDS` | `searchText`, `title`, `description`, `eventLocation` |
| `PUBLIC_SPONSOR_SEARCH_FIELDS` | `searchText`, `name`, `companyName`, `tagline`, `description`, `type` |

| Search UI | Match these fields |
|-----------|-------------------|
| Tenant / org picker | `organizationName`, `tenantId`, `domain` (parallel, merge) |
| Event picker / public `/events` / gallery events | `PUBLIC_EVENT_SEARCH_FIELDS` + numeric `id`; local fallback must be the same display fields |
| User / contact picker | firstName, lastName, email, userId |
| Settings / resource lists | display name **and** business key / id |
| Public `/sponsors` catalog | `PUBLIC_SPONSOR_SEARCH_FIELDS`; pick still commits `name`; Enter still commits typed text |
| Public `/gallery` albums | `PUBLIC_GALLERY_ALBUM_SEARCH_FIELDS` + numeric `id` |
| Public `/polls` | `title`, `description`, id (no `searchText` column) |
| Public `/focus-groups` | client-only: `searchText`, `name`, `slug`, `description`, id — no server `.contains` |

```typescript
// ✅ DO: same fields for menu (page 0, size 20) and listing (page/size)
fetchPublicTypeahead({ resource: 'event-details', query, containsFields: PUBLIC_EVENT_SEARCH_FIELDS, extraParams });
fetchPublicSearchPage({ resource: 'event-details', query, containsFields: PUBLIC_EVENT_SEARCH_FIELDS, extraParams, page, size });
```

```typescript
// ❌ DON'T: blob-only — empty search_text → empty grid after Enter
containsFields: ['searchText']
params.append('searchText.contains', trimmed);
```

### Why this matters (Tenant ID fix)

Typing `ten` must surface orgs whose **`tenantId`** contains `ten` (e.g. `tenant_demo_002` / Techies US).  
Typing `techie` must still match **`organizationName`** (“Techies US”).

**Broken:** server only sent `organizationName.contains` → `ten` showed “No matching organizations” even though `tenant_demo_002` exists.  
**Fixed:** parallel criteria, then merge/dedupe:

```typescript
// ✅ DO: searchTenantOrganizationsForSelectServer
const [byName, byTenantId] = await Promise.all([
  fetchTenantOrganizations(page, { search: trimmed, ...sort }),           // organizationName.contains
  fetchTenantOrganizations(page, { tenantIdContains: trimmed, ...sort }), // tenantId.contains
]);
return mergeOrganizationsByKey(byTenantId.data, byName.data).slice(0, LIMIT);
```

- Add `tenantIdContains` → `tenantId.contains` in [`fetchTenantOrganizations`](mdc:src/app/admin/tenant-management/organizations/ApiServerActions.ts) / [`TenantOrganizationFilters`](mdc:src/app/admin/tenant-management/types.ts).
- Client local filter should also match name **and** id (and domain when available).
- After server returns, **merge** with local matches so an empty name-only response never blanks good ID hits already in cache.

Apply the **same idea** to any new typeahead: identify the human label fields + stable id/key fields, query both (or filter both client-side when the dataset is small), merge, cap (~20). Public OCR-backed listings use **parallel structured fields plus `searchText`**, not `searchText` alone.

